 coriander", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "coarsely chopped fresh coriander", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 20, "raw": "Good quality tortilla chips", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "good quality tortilla chips", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To prepare beans either cover with water and soak overnight or cover with water and bring to a boil; boil 2 minutes and allow to sit in water for 1 hour. After soaking beans, drain off soaking water. Cover beans with fresh water and cover pot. Bring to boil. Add ½ cup chopped onion, garlic, ½ teaspoon cumin. Cover and simmer until beans are tender, about 1 hour. Drain."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place beans in food processor with ¾ teaspoon cumin, 1 ½ tablespoons chili powder, vinegar, butter, tomato paste, coriander and hot pepper sauce. Process until mixture is smooth. Adjust seasoning and add salt and pepper to taste."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Peel avocados and mash coarsely with lemon juice, salt and pepper to taste."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Mix sour cream with 1 tablespoon chili powder, ¼ teaspoon cumin."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Chop tomatoes."}, {"position": 6, "text": "To serve, place a layer of the bean mixture in a shallow serving dish. Top with mashed avocados, then with sour cream mixture. Sprinkle tomatoes evenly over sour cream; sprinkle on scallions, olives and cheese and top with fresh coriander."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Serve with tortilla chips."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 231.8, "protein_g": 8.2, "carbohydrates_g": 15.5, "fat_g": 16.3, "saturated_fat_g": 7.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 32.4, "sodium_mg": 259.5, "fiber_g": 5.0, "sugar_g": 2.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["appetizer"